    199  0758							; ---------------------------------------------------------
    200  0758							; The seam: player 1 moves to the guard of the band
    201  0758							; below. The count zcnt reaches 0 in line B1 of the course
    202  0758							; c of the seam (main.asm: p1_bands); from there to the end
    203  0758							; of line A0 of course c + 1 player 1 draws nothing, and
    204  0758							; these lines do in turn what the kernel needs to move it:
    205  0758							;   B1  (the rest)  prepares A2 as B1 does
    206  0758							;   A2  reads PF1 and PF2 of course c + 1, prepares B2,
    207  0758							;	 REFP1 of the guard below
    208  0758							;   B2  prepares A3 and the figure of Sir Roderick for B3
    209  0758							;   A3  waits zcoarse x 5 cycles, then RESP1: the coarse
    210  0758							;	 column (15 pixels per 5 cycles; RESP1 writes a cycle
    211  0758							;	 after place's, so the count and the fine move are
    212  0758							;	 place's for the column - 3)
    213  0758							;   B3  HMOVE first: the fine move (HMP1, written in the HUD
    214  0758							;	 after HMCLR, SC_HM); its comb blanks pixels 0-7 of
    215  0758							;	 this line, which is the mortar of block column 0
    216  0758							;	 (never in the courses of the openings); the pointer
    217  0758							;	 of the graphics of the guard below; PF2 of course
    218  0758							;	 c + 1 (in its window, after the right half)
    219  0758							;   A0  as A0, and the pointer of the colours
    220  0758							; then back to the end of A0, and the kernel goes on with
    221  0758							; the guard below. Sir Roderick is drawn in every line.
    222  0758
